---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, AUTHOR } from '../consts';
const url = new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href;
const schema = [{ '@type': 'ProfilePage', '@id': url, url, mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#james` } }];
---
<Base title={`About ${AUTHOR.name} | ${SITE.name}`} description={`${AUTHOR.name} has 13+ years in B2B marketing, SEO and agency account management. About him and The Account Brief.`} schema={schema}>
  <header class="article-head narrow">
    {AUTHOR.photo && <img class="about-photo" src={AUTHOR.photo} alt={AUTHOR.name} width="112" height="112" />}
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>{AUTHOR.name}</h1>
    <p class="lede">I write The Account Brief: practical notes on B2B marketing strategy and client service, from the person who runs the account.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose narrow">
    <p>
      I've spent more than 13 years in digital marketing, B2B growth and SEO. Today I'm a Client Services Manager, working in
      Birmingham, UK. I've founded a start-up, worked in-house and worked across numerous agencies, so I've seen B2B
      marketing from both sides of the client relationship: writing the strategy, sitting in the client meeting and delivering the work.
    </p>
    <h2>Why this blog</h2>
    <p>
      Most B2B marketing advice is written by vendors or in-house teams. Far less comes from the account side: the person
      who has to turn a strategy into results a client will renew for. That's the gap The Account Brief fills.
    </p>
    <h2>What I write about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/category/b2b-strategy/">B2B strategy</a>: frameworks, budgets and KPIs that hold up in practice.</li>
      <li><a href="/category/key-account-management/">Key account management</a>: account plans, QBRs and growing accounts.</li>
      <li><a href="/category/client-services/">Client services</a>: onboarding, reporting, retention and difficult conversations.</li>
      <li><a href="/category/b2b-seo/">B2B SEO</a>: SEO that moves pipeline, and how to report it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Examples are drawn from real work, with clients anonymised.</p>
    {AUTHOR.linkedin && <p>The best place to reach me is <a href={AUTHOR.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>.</p>}
  </div>
</Base>
